  "about": "Shared personal-information (PII) test vectors — kid safety, CONTRACT §12.4. Used by tests/server-e2e.mjs (server/lib/ChatFilter.php, via the API and the PHP CLI) and, embedded by tools/build.mjs as window.__BUILD__.piiVectors, by the developer center self-tests (60-social.js G.sys.social.maskPII).  whole: the entire text must become 🔒 · partial: some 🔒 and no 4-digit run left · keep: innocent kid sentences that must come back unchanged · leak: adversarial disguises — none of `secrets` may survive (compared after a strong normalisation: NFKC, every digit script → ASCII, invisible/format/marks removed, letters and digits only, lower-case) · nickname: names the account rules must reject / allow. tests/server-e2e.mjs runs all of them on the server (PHP CLI + API), tests/pii-client.mjs in the built game (G.sys.social.maskPII) and diffs client vs server output. Keep the client and the server rules in sync: both must pass every vector.",
